Blackdrift: Safe Browsing is off and the settings no longer offer it.

Why: Blackdrift is built without a Google Safe Browsing API key (AppConstants
MOZ_GOOGLE_SAFEBROWSING_API_KEY is the placeholder), so Gecko's
SafeBrowsing.sys.mjs clears the update and gethash URLs of the google,
google4 and google5 providers. No malware or phishing list is ever
downloaded, and the switch "Block potentially dangerous and deceptive
sites" protected nothing while claiming it did.

- Settings.shouldUseSafeBrowsing() always returns false, so
  EngineProvider.setupSafeBrowsing() sets SafeBrowsingPolicy.NONE on every
  engine start (GeckoEngine itself starts at RECOMMENDED). The stored
  "pref_safe_browsing" value is no longer read, so a user upgrading from a
  build where it was true (the default) also gets NONE.
- The switch, its SafeBrowsingSwitchPreference class, its preference key,
  the settings-change listener and telemetry branches and the English
  title and summary are removed. Translations keep their now-unused
  strings (lint ExtraTranslation is ignored); SupportUtils.
  getSafeBrowsingURL() stays because patch 0204 rewrites it.
- The instrumented SafeBrowsingTest is deleted and SettingsPrivacyMenuRobot
  no longer looks for the switch.

Tracking protection is untouched: it uses the Mozilla provider and the
*-track-digest256 lists, configured through the tracking protection
policy, not the Safe Browsing categories. GeckoView's
ContentBlocking.Settings.setSafeBrowsingProviders() is left at its
default: with no API key and the categories at NONE the google providers
do nothing, and clearing them would only change runtime prefs that cannot
be checked without a device.

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

